  {
   "id": "gkzQT50PCAAJ",
   "from": "Joshua Rosenberg",
   "author": "6a3b5e8bc43576e6",
   "date": "2018-05-25T17:22:02Z",
   "subject": "Re: TidyLPA Support",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">J.D., thanks so much. Jaclyn, I&#39;d like to look into this more with my collaborators, though I think it may be a good bit of time before we do implement it (if we do). I should ask, do you have and use MPlus? Because if you do, it may be easier (for now - and I don&#39;t like to say this!) to do this exclusively there. Also, my guess is that we&#39;d only be able to implement this for the tidyLPA functions that use MPlus. So, unfortunately, given the two tools that the package provides an interface to (the mclust R package and MPlus), I think that MPlus may be necessary. There are some other options (like <a href=\"http://openmx.psyc.virginia.edu/docs/OpenMx/latest/NewBeginnersGuide.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://openmx.psyc.virginia.edu/docs/OpenMx/latest/NewBeginnersGuide.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496187150000&amp;usg=AOvVaw22C09wEUt8_o_XIxZsJge4\">the OpenMx R package</a> or <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/EasyMx/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/EasyMx/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496187150000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0koJNHUlSQxi8Eeq5vsz93\">the EasyMx package</a> that provides an interface to it), but that would (at least from my vantage) require a substantial initial investment of time (in part because while the other options are flexible, they are pretty challenging to start to use).<div>Josh</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Thu, May 24, 2018 at 9:51 AM J.D. Haltigan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jhal...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I have experience with the 3-step, Josh. The attached may be of use as a starting point.</div><div><br></div><div>Best regards,<br></div><div>J.D.<br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, May 24, 2018 at 9:40 AM, Joshua Rosenberg <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jro...@msu.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Jaclyn, do you have the MPlus syntax for carrying out this approach (I bet I can find this in the MPlus manual, too)?</div><div><br></div>Does anyone (Dan, J.D., Caspar) have any experience with this three-step approach? This isn&#39;t implemented as part of tidyLPA, and I&#39;m curious about how difficult it may be to do so. <div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Josh<br><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Wed, May 23, 2018 at 8:54 PM Jaclyn Swinton &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Jaclyn....@anu.edu.au</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:12pt;color:#000000;font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif\" dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"></p>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">\r\n<font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hi, </span></font></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">\r\n<font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><br>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">\r\n<font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">My name is Jaci and I&#39;m a student at ANU. <font size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">I&#39;m\r\n currently analysing data using latent profile analysis and am using the tidyLPA package in conjunction with mclust to do so. I was hoping to get some help about conducting a 3-step LPA.</span></font><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">  (1) I have\r\n 3 continuous variables from which I would like to predict latent profiles. I would additionally like to (2) </span></font><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">use predictor variables to create latent class probabilities for the most likely latent\r\n class membership, as well as (3) using these latent profiles as a predictor of distal outcomes. </span></font></span></font></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">\r\n<font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><br>\r\n</span></font></span></font></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">\r\n<font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">Unfortunately I haven&#39;t been\r\n able to find any syntax which enables me to conduct steps 2 and 3 in r and I was wondering whether this is possible with the mclust/tidy package?</span></font></span></font></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">\r\n<font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><br>\r\n</span></font></span></font></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">\r\n<font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">Many thanks in advance for any help. </span></font></span></font></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">\r\n<font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><br>\r\n</span></font></span></font></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">\r\n<font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><font size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">Jaci Swinton</span></font></span></font></div>\r\n<br>\r\n<p></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;tidyLPA&quot; group.<br></blockquote></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div>"
